Hi <%= @notice.name %> admins,

We've added Workspace domain validation for Google sign-in in Firezone. For new
providers, verification with a Workspace administrator saves the verified domains
and enables validation automatically. Verification with a personal Google
account creates a personal-only provider.

Your existing Google provider will stay as it is. No action is required to keep
existing sign-ins working. If you'd like to restrict sign-ins to verified
Workspace domains, you can enable validation by verifying those domains and
saving the provider. Editing its name or session lifetimes does not enable
domain validation.

You can also add separate Google providers for different Workspace organizations,
while keeping one personal or existing unrestricted provider. Workspace domain
lists cannot overlap within your Firezone account.

Your Firezone account <%= @notice.slug %> has stored Google identities using these
email domains:
<%= for domain <- @notice.domains do %>
- <%= domain %>
<% end %>
These are observed email domains, not a verified Workspace domain list. Review
them when setting up validation; Firezone obtains the verified domain list
from Google.
<%= if @notice.consumer_identity_count > 0 do %>

We also found <%= @notice.consumer_identity_count %> Google identities using consumer email addresses in
this account. If you choose to restrict your existing provider, arrange a
separate sign-in option for these personal accounts.
<% end %>

HOW TO ENABLE DOMAIN RESTRICTIONS

1. Open Settings -> Authentication in your Firezone account:
   <%= @settings_url %>
   Add a new Google provider to keep the existing provider unchanged, or edit
   the existing provider to restrict it.

2. Click Verify Now. Sign in as a Google Workspace administrator and grant
   read-only access to your organization's domain list.

3. Review Verified domains. If users sign in from other Workspace organizations,
   click Verify another domain and complete verification as an administrator of
   each organization. They can all use the same provider and sign-in option.

4. Before clicking Save, check that the list covers the Workspace domains your
   users need. Saving enables the restrictions.

Personal Google accounts cannot use a provider with verified-domain
restrictions. This includes personal Google accounts that use a company email
address. They need your account's personal Google provider, an existing
unrestricted provider, or another authentication method.

See the Google authentication guide for details:
https://www.firezone.dev/kb/authenticate/google

If you need help, contact support@firezone.dev or reach out in your support
channel.
